Original commit body from 20dd0dc9b3826e068a3d5acb67bd15dfd659727f:

INV-komoj seeds a caller only on the variables its call defines at the
result positions the returned value occupies. Go's def/use extractor drops
the blank identifier, so `_, err := get()` defined ("err",) against an
arity of two, the position rule could not apply, and the fallback seeded
every variable -- err included, which the caller returns, so the lift
climbed the error chain.

DefUseResult and CfgStatement gain `targets`, the left-hand side by
position with the blank kept as `_`; Go's short-var and assignment
handlers report it when a blank is present and every other target names
exactly one variable (`*p, _ = f()` keeps the fallback). stmt_defuse uses
it where present, so the received position maps exactly and a value that
lands in the blank seeds nothing.

Corpus A/B (dev e3ea9db6c9; runc, gin, coredns, buildah): 0 verdicts
moved; buildah walks 2874 -> 2749 (e.g. mkcw.go `imageID, _, _, err :=`
no longer seeds imageID and err), host-secret-no-network evidence 91 ->
79 with shorter source_returned_by chains; runc, gin, coredns unchanged.
Not covered: `var _, err = f()` declarations.

